                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm really lovin' that retro gem!\n \nBut be warned, this game is currently lacking the Tag \"Difficult\" ... it's really one heck of a example for \"easy to learn, hard to master\"!\n \nHELI COMMANDO and Dark Souls have more in common as you might think first place:\n- There's no tutorial, you have to learn by yourself\n- Unforgiving, there's no \"health\" or \"shield\" or such pussy things. You hit something, you die.\n- You  will die a lot ...\n- When you die, the entire level resets\n- You can't freely save, the game gives you jumpcodes every couple of levels\n- The feeling after mastering a level you played and failed like 10 times is incredibly rewarding!!\n \nDon't get me wrong here, I meant this absolutely in a positive way :-)\nThe only enemy in this game is YOU. Sounds crazy? Here's why you crash your heli first place:\n- you are too greedy\nor\n- you are too cocky\nor maybe\n- you've been unconcentrated for just too long\n \nWhen you want to collect everything to let your highscore skyrocket, you really have to think ahead and try to stay calm and focused all the time. Ah, I forgot to mention: You're constantly running out of fuel and have to refuel at specific places that are placed all around the level. You really should look out for them and plan your next action accordingly. \n \nSince I'm an 80s kid I grew up with games like this and imidiately was reminded about that in the second the intro sound of HELI COMMAND kicked in. The music is very authentic such as almost every ingame sound, totally 8-Bit, totally arcade.\n \nI play with an XBOX 360 Gamepad, you get used to the controls really quickly ;-)\n \nIf you like nostalgica retro action with unique style (no Unity hehe) and awesome audio, that's difficult, no ... it's hard and feel like playing a game that might just have come out of an arcade gaming machine ... then this game IS TOTALLY FOR YOU! \n \nWorth a look, maybe there'll be a demo in the future so give it a try!\n \n",
